    <item>
      <title>2.6.4</title>
      <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 21:24:52 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>13</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.6.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h2&gt;ReadingPaper 2.6.4&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quotations look like quotations again.&lt;/strong&gt; Some newsletters quote a source at
length, and that formatting was being lost on the way into the reader — the quoted paragraphs ran
flush against the writer's own, with nothing to show where one ended and the other began. Where
it's possible to tell, they're set apart properly now.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/allenmhc/ReadingPaper-releases/releases/download/v2.6.4/ReadingPaper-2.6.4.dmg" length="6591326" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="xoKc1+YnIJf/Mj9iea6KJWQV6xrvuJxhAHvvqCD7/7TGWDmXVgYvMxaNLunwX+YK4uFjvr3tAuKoIpXmJ7C3Cg==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2.6.3</title>
      <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:14:27 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>12</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.6.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h2&gt;ReadingPaper 2.6.3&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintenance release.&lt;/strong&gt; Nothing changes in the app you read in. This one only
makes a locally built copy look different from an installed one, so the two don't get mixed up
while the app is being worked on.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/allenmhc/ReadingPaper-releases/releases/download/v2.6.3/ReadingPaper-2.6.3.dmg" length="6589811" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="5ETRXKZw8+A1jq8OmNU3xSenf3jiQ28thOOm0MPEMDgEPvSBmQ3Qi0HpIJSDAZEIsskLT3UtKdA0qbNjc1EvAQ==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2.6.1</title>
      <pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:15:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>10</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.6.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h2&gt;ReadingPaper 2.6.1&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improved article parsing.&lt;/strong&gt; Some newsletters carry sections the reader has to
reconstruct client-side, and one arrangement wasn't being recognised — it came through as loose
text and images. It now renders as intended.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/allenmhc/ReadingPaper-releases/releases/download/v2.6.1/ReadingPaper-2.6.1.dmg" length="6586047" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="b7ej69ijxM3vR5vnQegRYa8PbDxuxLDhwT0Qo8YLoiP4hFOshoZrzqqpPU7BgFAVZzxrZ4kW1DHH/TwijoKHDg==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2.6.0</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 07:10:41 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>9</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.6.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h2&gt;ReadingPaper 2.6.0&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Four themes, and they now colour the whole window.&lt;/strong&gt; White, sepia, gray and black
— the same set Instapaper offers on the web and on iOS — chosen from swatches painted in the theme
they select.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Its own settings page.&lt;/strong&gt; The theme is no longer buried in Reader settings:
      it's &lt;em&gt;View ▸ Theme…&lt;/em&gt; (⌥⌘T), also on the reader toolbar and in the account menu.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The whole pane, not just the article.&lt;/strong&gt; The strip behind the toolbar and the
      top and bottom of the article list used to stay white whatever you were reading in. Now the
      window is one continuous field of colour, with the list and the toolbar floating on top
      of it.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A contrasting article list.&lt;/strong&gt; Each theme draws the list in the opposite tone —
      charcoal beside white paper, espresso beside sepia, off-white beside gray and black — so the
      two panes stay distinct instead of blending into one another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whatever you were reading in carries over: the old light and dark themes become white and black.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/allenmhc/ReadingPaper-releases/releases/download/v2.6.0/ReadingPaper-2.6.0.dmg" length="6584622" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="VwchNUjaIE/WI9hh7CRbtKGs3j5CsFyA2PZBx/ksvl1urIrDH1VOYFGUsQ8JUtnw6IydqmZtGIZVwtPKeAypDA==" />
    </item>
